  "holm_bonferroni_note": "Holm-Bonferroni (alpha=0.05 family-wise) applied across the 9 generator dedup p-values from a single canonical random key (audit of the UNMARKED corpora); none reject, as expected for unmarked output.",
  "verdict": {
    "bottleneck_binds_for": [
      "WyLLM-vanilla-DiffCSP++"
    ],
    "criterion": "naive FPR on unmarked corpus exceeds 5x nominal alpha (1e-3), driven by design_effect > 1 (collision classes inflating the effective sample size below n)",
    "frontier_crossings": "none of the 9 generators or 3 reference populations fall below the auditability frontier N* at gamma=0.5 for any m in {4,6,8,16}: even the most repetitive generator, WyLLM-vanilla-DiffCSP++ (n_eff=300.3), is far above the largest frontier N*=18 (m=4). The bottleneck therefore does not manifest as an outright audit infeasibility for these released generators -- it manifests as false-positive-rate miscalibration of the naive (non-deduplicated) test, which BasinMark's deduplicated audit corrects.",
    "wyllm_vanilla_vs_mp20train": {
      "WyLLM-vanilla-DiffCSP++": {
