        "n_eff": 27136.0,
        "design_effect": 1.0109080188679245,
        "fpr_naive": 0.001,
        "fpr_dedup": 0.002
      },
      "interpretation": "WyLLM-vanilla-DiffCSP++ collapses to 649/999 (64.96%) distinct fingerprints, the most repetitive generator in the corpus, versus MP20_train's 27049/27136 (99.68%). This drives WyLLM-vanilla's design effect to 4.32 (vs 1.01 for MP20_train) and its naive FPR to 0.064 at nominal alpha=1e-3 -- a 64x inflation -- while the deduplicated test stays at 0.0000, i.e. calibrated at or below nominal. This is the cleanest empirical demonstration in the corpus that deduplication, not raw structure count, is what calibration depends on."
